From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dxcore: adapter factory, lists and adapters over DXGI

DXCoreCreateAdapterFactory was a stub that returned E_NOINTERFACE, so
everything built on DXCore -- DirectML, ONNX Runtime and Windows ML
device selection, PyTorch's DirectML backend, programs choosing a GPU for
compute -- found no adapter.

- The factory is one object per process. CreateAdapterList gives the
  adapters with every attribute asked for: Direct3D 11 graphics (all of
  DXGI's adapters), Direct3D 12 graphics and core compute (where d3d12
  can make a device for the adapter, asked once); no attributes is
  E_INVALIDARG. GetAdapterByLuid; event registration for list-stale,
  adapter-removed and budget events (kept; adapters do not come and go
  while a process runs here).
- Adapter lists: GetAdapter, GetAdapterCount, IsStale (the adapters DXGI
  has now against the list's), Sort by Hardware, MinimumPower and
  HighPerformance (stable, first deciding preference wins),
  IsAdapterPreferenceSupported, GetFactory.
- An adapter is the same object however it is found. Its properties:
  instance LUID, driver version (the user-mode driver's), description,
  hardware ID and its parts, kernel driver model (from D3DKMT, else
  WDDM 2.6), preemption granularity (DMA buffer), dedicated adapter and
  system memory, shared memory, ACG compatible, hardware, integrated,
  detachable; sizes, too-small buffers (E_INVALIDARG) and unknown
  properties (DXGI_ERROR_INVALID_CALL) as documented. QueryState: the
  memory budget of a node's local or non-local segments
  (IDXGIAdapter3::QueryVideoMemoryInfo) and driver updates (none); no
  state can be set.

Gate: test/dxcore-gate.sh (Xvfb, test/dxcore-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_D3D12_ATTRIBUTE, SG_MUTANT_NEW_ADAPTER
(dxcore/main.c).
---
--- a/dlls/dxcore/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/dxcore/Makefile.in
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 MODULE = dxcore.dll
+IMPORTS = dxgi gdi32 uuid
 
 EXTRADLLFLAGS = -Wb,--prefer-native
 
--- a/dlls/dxcore/main.c
+++ b/dlls/dxcore/main.c
@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
